From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chromium-blink-ios <noreply@github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] iOS extensions: context-scoped authorization for single-process coexistence

In single-process Blink on iOS, every document and service worker shares one
RenderProcessHost ID while extensions::ProcessMap stores at most one ExtensionId
per process. Whichever extension claims the slot first locks every other enabled
extension out of private subresource loads, service worker registration, API
dispatch, messaging, event listeners, and event classification.

Under content::RenderProcessHost::run_renderer_in_process(), authorize each
boundary strictly from browser-owned context identity (factory initiator origin,
committed non-sandboxed RenderFrameHost, tracked WorkerId, or ServiceWorkerTaskQueue
activation token) without broadening ProcessMap globally, preserving isolation
against web pages and sandboxed frames.

